   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Light Tunnel\n\nA forward flight through a tunnel of luminous, twisting light ribbons with a halftone texture and a soft defocused vanishing point, drawn in WebGL.\n\nCategory: shaders. Length: 3 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A title reveal or product intro needs a luminous forward flight through a tunnel.\n- Light ribbons should have perspective, depth and soft atmospheric glow.\n\nAvoid when:\n- A quiet background should leave attention on dense UI: use shader-mesh-gradient.\n- You need a flat liquid distortion instead of forward flight: use shader-warp.\n\nVariables:\n- speed (number, 0-5): Speed, default 1\n- twist (number, 0-2): Twist, default 0.7\n- spirals (number, 1-6): Spirals, default 3\n- glow (number, 0-3): Glow, default 1\n- depth (number, 0.5-2): Depth, default 1\n- time_offset (number, 0-60): Start time, default 0\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.5\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
